			"Message": "chore(Project): Update editor element submodules to enforce PascalCase naming and consolidate lint configurations\n\nUpdate all tracked editor elements (Air, Common, Echo, Grove, Maintain, Mist, Mountain, SideCar) to their latest revisions. The primary focus is the removal of blanket lint allowances (`non_snake_case`, `non_camel_case_types`, `non_upper_case_globals`) that were masking violations of the project-wide PascalCase naming convention.\n\n**Specific Changes:**\n- **Air, Common, Mountain, SideCar:** Remove broad suppression directives from binary and core modules, enforcing strict casing for functions, variables, and structs.\n- **Mist:** Consolidate lint exceptions into `lib.rs` to reduce visual clutter in individual source files.\n- **Grove:** Re-enable specific `non_snake_case` allowance in `main.rs` to preserve FFI compatibility for transport constants.\n- **Vine (Mountain):** Strip generated lint suppressions from gRPC bindings to ensure generated IPC code adheres to project standards.\n- **Maintain:** Update Rust documentation submodule to Nightly 1.97.0.\n- **Echo:** Sync Rust documentation submodule.\n\nThese changes unify the codebase styling, ensure lints are active for all standard identifiers, and centralize necessary FFI exceptions.",
